{
 "esm": "1.2.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "GWDOMomentumTendency",
  "description": "What GWDO returns to the model: the wind tendencies and the surface stress. Lines 594-662 of `phys/physics_mmm/bl_gwdo.F90` (WRF 4.8, NCAR/MMM-physics CCPP kernel `bl_gwdo_run`).\n\nThe drag on a layer is the DIVERGENCE OF THE STRESS the wave and the blocked flow carry across it. In pressure coordinates that is -g dtau/dp, and the scheme writes it as (tau[k+1] - tau[k]) g / del[k] -- a conservative finite-volume difference of an interface flux. It is written here as `D(taup, wrt: lev)` on the column-mass coordinate ze = (p_i[1] - p_i)/g that the column stage already built, lowered by the EarthSciDiscretizations `face_flux_D_lev_supplied_faces` rule; the layer measure dz is then del/g and the rule reproduces the Fortran difference exactly. The column-integrated stress is the same operator's adjoint, the whole-column integral of the tendency against that measure, lowered by `integral_lev_whole`. Nothing here is a hand-written stencil.\n\nTWO LIMITERS, and they are a legitimate part of the tendency rather than a time-stepping device -- but they are parameterised BY the time step. The first prevents the drag from reversing the wind within one step: it scales the tendency down until |dtau| dt does not exceed the projected wind speed. The second reduces the drag in the mesosphere by the ratio of the local density to 0.01 kg/m^3, above 7.5 hPa. Both therefore make `deltim` a PARAMETER OF THE TENDENCY, not the integrator's step, and a document that mounts this component must prescribe it rather than inherit it -- the same situation as WSM6's operator-split sub-step. On the reference set neither limiter ever binds: over all 5250 dumped columns and 262500 cells the damping factor is exactly 1, so the tendency there is the unlimited stress divergence and the limiter branches are carried but untested. That is stated in the test descriptions rather than hidden.\n\nThe tendency is an OBSERVED and the wind is not owned here. WRF's own interface is in-out -- `rublten` arrives carrying the PBL tendency and leaves carrying PBL plus GWDO -- but GWDO's own contribution is a rate, `dtaux3d`, that the scheme computes and returns separately, so this component exposes exactly that and adds nothing to it. A coupled document adds it to whatever else drives the wind.\n\nThe final rotation takes the tendencies from earth-relative back onto the model grid, undoing the rotation the column stage applied to the wind on the way in.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "wrf",
   "gravity-wave-drag",
   "gwdo",
   "momentum-tendency",
   "column"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "Hong, S.-Y., and co-authors (2025). Revision of the orographic gravity wave drag parameterization in the KIAPS Integrated Model. Wea. Forecasting."
   },
   {
    "citation": "Kim, Y.-J., and A. Arakawa (1995). Improvement of orographic gravity wave parameterization using a mesoscale gravity wave model. J. Atmos. Sci. 52, 1875-1902.",
    "doi": "10.1175/1520-0469(1995)052<1875:IOOGWP>2.0.CO;2"
   },
   {
    "citation": "NCAR/MMM-physics bl_gwdo.F90 at commit 52cfbd7 (WRF 4.8 phys/physics_mmm submodule)."
   }
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 50,
   "description": "Number of model layers (WRF kte). Bound at the mount edge and passed down to the imported grid, to the two lowering rules and to the `blk` subsystem beneath."
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "GWDOMomentumTendency": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/face_flux_D_lev_supplied_faces.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/integral_lev_whole.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    }
   ],
   "subsystems": {
    "wrf": {
     "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_constants.esm"
    },
    "par": {
     "ref": "./gwdo_parameters.esm"
    },
    "blk": {
     "ref": "./blocking_drag.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    }
   },
   "variables": {
    "deltim": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "s",
     "description": "The time step the two limiters are scaled against. It is a PARAMETER OF THE TENDENCY, not the integrator's step: the wind-reversal limiter asks whether the drag would reverse the wind within one model step, so the tendency GWDO returns depends on how long the host intends to apply it. A document that mounts this component prescribes it explicitly."
    },
    "kgwdmax": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "NLEV/2 in integer arithmetic, read from the mounted column state: the level at which the wind-reversal limiter hands over to the mesosphere density limiter."
    },
    "sina": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Sine of the map-rotation angle, read from the mounted column state."
    },
    "cosa": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Cosine of the map-rotation angle, read from the mounted column state."
    },
    "xn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Zonal component of the unit vector along the low-level wind, read from the launch stage; zero where the column produces no drag."
    },
    "yn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Meridional component of the same unit vector."
    },
    "taup": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "Pa",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Total interface stress -- saturating wave plus flow blocking -- read from the blocking stage. Bound to a bare interface-shaped observed of this document so that the face-flux divergence rule matches it."
    },
    "ze": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "The column-mass vertical coordinate, read from the column state: the air mass per unit area below each interface. The stress divergence and the column integral below are both taken with respect to it."
    },
    "dz": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Layer mass per unit area, del/g, read from the column state. It is the measure both imported rules read by bare name; with it, `D(taup, wrt: lev)` IS the Fortran's (taup[k+1] - taup[k]) g / del[k] and `integral(f, var: lev)` IS its sum f del / g."
    },
    "prsl": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "Pa",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Layer mid-point pressure, read from the column state; the mesosphere limiter is gated on it."
    },
    "rho": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/m^3",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Air density, read from the column state; the mesosphere limiter scales by it."
    },
    "velco": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Projected wind speed at the layer interface, read from the column state. The wind-reversal limiter compares the momentum the drag would remove in one step against it."
    },
    "taud_raw": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Unlimited drag on the layer: the divergence of the interface stress, -g dtau/dp."
    },
    "taud_safe": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "taud_raw with values below the qmin threshold replaced by qmin itself, so that the limiter's reciprocal is finite everywhere. Wherever the substitution acts, the limiter's own `|taud| >= qmin` test has already selected the unlimited branch, so it cannot reach an answer."
    },
    "denfac": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Mesosphere density reduction min(rho/pcutoff_den, 1), which falls below one only above about 7.5 hPa where the air is thinner than 0.01 kg/m^3."
    },
    "dtfac_raw": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "The damping factor as the two limiter loops compute it: the wind-reversal form below kgwdmax, the density-scaled form from kgwdmax to NLEV-1 and only where the pressure is at or below pcutoff, and one elsewhere."
    },
    "dtfac": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "The damping factor as the Fortran's array finally holds it: dtfac_raw below the top layer, and dtfac_raw[NLEV-1] copied into the top layer, which is what `dtfac(:,kte) = dtfac(:,kte-1)` does. On the whole reference set it is EXACTLY 1 in all 262500 cells -- neither limiter binds anywhere -- so the limiter branches are transcribed but not exercised by any test here.",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "taud": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Limited drag on the layer, taud_raw dtfac."
    },
    "dtaux2d": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Earth-relative zonal wind tendency: the drag is anti-parallel to the low-level wind, so it is the drag magnitude times that direction's zonal component."
    },
    "dtauy2d": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Earth-relative meridional wind tendency."
    },
    "dusfc": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "Pa",
     "description": "Earth-relative zonal surface stress: minus the mass-weighted column integral of the zonal tendency, which is the momentum per unit area per unit time the scheme removes from the column and hands to the ground."
    },
    "dvsfc": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "Pa",
     "description": "Earth-relative meridional surface stress."
    },
    "dtaux3d": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "GRID-relative zonal wind tendency -- the scheme's primary output, added to `rublten` by the WRF wrapper. It is an instantaneous rate, not an increment over a step."
    },
    "dtauy3d": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Grid-relative meridional wind tendency, the scheme's other primary output."
    },
    "dusfcg": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "Pa",
     "description": "Grid-relative zonal surface stress (WRF `DUSFCG`)."
    },
    "dvsfcg": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "Pa",
     "description": "Grid-relative meridional surface stress (WRF `DVSFCG`)."
    },
    "z_sfc": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/m^2",
     "description": "Lower boundary of the column, ze[1]: the free name the EarthSciDiscretizations column_nonuniform_1d integral rules match as the lower bound of a bottom-anchored integral (ESD #39)."
    },
    "z_top": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/m^2",
     "description": "Upper boundary of the column, ze[NLEV+1]: the free name the EarthSciDiscretizations column_nonuniform_1d integral rules match as the upper bound of a top-anchored integral (ESD #39)."
    }
   },
   "equations": [
    {
     "lhs": "deltim",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "input_deltim",
      "args": []
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "kgwdmax",
     "rhs": "blk.sat.oro.col.kgwdmax"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "sina",
     "rhs": "blk.sat.oro.col.sina"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "cosa",
     "rhs": "blk.sat.oro.col.cosa"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "xn",
     "rhs": "blk.sat.oro.xn"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "yn",
     "rhs": "blk.sat.oro.yn"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "taup",
     "rhs": "blk.taup"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "ze",
     "rhs": "blk.sat.oro.col.ze"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "dz",
     "rhs": "blk.sat.oro.col.dz"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "prsl",
     "rhs": "blk.sat.oro.col.prsl"
    },
    {
